      "id": "f71ecb3c-d500-4a6c-b40f-491f451a50e3",
      "name": "Enquiry form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -180
      ],
      "webhookId": "404c5e20-4ec3-448e-b69d-2a18cf76fef4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One shape for every channel. The form is only one door \u2014 email, SMS and phone\n// transcripts arrive via other triggers and are normalised to exactly this object,\n// so everything downstream reads the same fields regardless of where it came from.\n//\n// `raw` is never overwritten anywhere in the pipeline. Extraction can then be re-run\n// and compared later, which is what makes the prompt-version comparison possible.\nconst now = new Date().toISOString();\n\nreturn items.map((item, i) => {\n  const f = item.json;\n  return {\n    json: {\n      job_id: `JOB-${new Date().getFullYear()}-${String(Date.now()).slice(-4)}${i}`,\n      state: 'new',\n      created_at: now,\n      channel: f.channel ?? 'web-form',\n      raw: f.raw ?? '',\n      form_customer_name: f.customer_name ?? null,\n      form_email: f.email ?? null,\n      form_phone: f.phone ?? null,\n      form_address: f.address ?? null,\n      events: [],\n    },\n  };\n});"
      },
      "id": "84d89b6b-491c-4d18-9166-a18a8de3a2e2",
      "name": "Normalise inbound",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "text": "={{ $json.raw }}",
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"customer_name\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"email\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"phone\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"locality\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"language\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"de\",\n        \"en\",\n        \"fr\",\n        \"it\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"job_type\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"described_scope\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"urgency\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"emergency\",\n        \"urgent\",\n        \"scheduled\",\n        \"no_rush\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"deadline\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"in_service_area\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"boolean\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"is_repeat_customer\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"missing_fields\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"extraction_confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"disqualify_reason\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"language\",\n    \"urgency\",\n    \"missing_fields\",\n    \"extraction_confidence\"\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You extract structured data from enquiry messages sent to a private dental practice in canton St. Gallen, Switzerland. They arrive in German or English and are often incomplete.\n\nNever invent a value. If a field is not present, return null and name it in missing_fields. A plausible guess is worse than a null: a null gets asked about, a guess gets acted on.\n\nKeep described_scope in the language it was written in and set language accordingly.\n\nurgency is about consequence, not tone. A calm message can describe an emergency and an angry one can describe something trivial. For this business, treat as an emergency: A genuine emergency is a presentation with airway, bleeding or time-limited tissue risk: facial or submandibular swelling that is spreading, closing the eye, crossing the midline of the neck or accompanied by fever, trismus or difficulty swallowing or breathing; bleeding after an extraction that has not stopped after 30 minutes of firm pressure, especially in a patient on anticoagulants; and dental trauma in which a permanent tooth has been knocked out or displaced, where the reimplantation window is measured in tens of minutes. These must reach a clinician by voice immediately and must never sit in an automated triage queue, be answered by an auto-reply, or be offered the next available online slot. Severe pain alone is urgent but not an emergency; pain plus swelling plus fever is.\n\nService area \u2014 Geography matters far less here than for a trade contractor: the patient travels to the chair, not the other way round, so the boundary is about whether someone will realistically keep a recall appointment every six months rather than whether a van can reach them \u2014 a Wil or Bregenz commuter who passes through St. Gallen daily is a better fit than a Rorschach resident without a car, and the automation should never hard-reject on postcode alone.\nIn: St. Gallen, Gossau SG, Wittenbach, Goldach, Rorschach, Teufen AR, Flawil, Arbon TG. Out: Lugano, Geneva, Sion, Zermatt. If a locality is stated but you do not recognise it, return null rather than guessing \u2014 a wrong false loses real work.\n\nextraction_confidence is your honest estimate that a human reading the same text would extract the same fields. Do not inflate it.\n\nIf no actionable treatment is described at all, set job_type null and give a disqualify_reason."
        }
      },
