    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The escalation branch\n\nThis is the only unconditional exit from the automated path in W1.\n\nA genuine emergency is a presentation with airway, bleeding or time-limited tissue risk: facial or submandibular swelling that is spreading, closing the eye, crossing the midline of the neck or accompanied by fever, trismus or difficulty swallowing or breathing; bleeding after an extraction that has not stopped after 30 minutes of firm pressure, especially in a patient on anticoagulants; and dental trauma in which a permanent tooth has been knocked out or displaced, where the reimplantation window is measured in tens of minutes. These must reach a clinician by voice immediately and must never sit in an automated triage queue, be answered by an auto-reply, or be offered the next available online slot. Severe pain alone is urgent but not an emergency; pain plus swelling plus fever is.\n\nNone of that belongs in a pricing pipeline. If your triage ever routes one into the normal flow, **report it** \u2014 an automation that handles an emergency as routine admin is exactly the kind of boundary failure this thesis is about.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "ab9fe7f5-750a-4df9-84e6-6647f938f96b",
      "name": "Note 2",
